{
  "where_we_lag": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "In overlapping crude shares, Kanta-Häme's symptomatic treatment is 34.2% (95% CI 30.4–38.3) versus 39.5% nationally, and 32.1% (95% CI 28.3–36.1) versus 27.5% have no treatment record within 12 months.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "cty:symptomatic:Kanta_Hämeen_hyvinvointialue",
        "nat:symptomatic",
        "cty:no_treatment_record:Kanta_Hämeen_hyvinvointialue",
        "nat:no_treatment_record",
        "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Kanta-Häme's crude symptomatic treatment share is 34.2% (95% CI 30.4–38.3; n=187/546) compared with 39.5% (5871/14873) nationally, and the 95% confidence interval excludes the national value.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:symptomatic:Kanta_Hämeen_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:symptomatic"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Kanta-Häme's crude share with no treatment record within 12 months is 32.1% (95% CI 28.3–36.1; n=175/546) versus 27.5% (4089/14873) nationally, with the 95% confidence interval excluding the national value; because this category mixes untreated patients and unrecorded treatment, low treatment shares may partly reflect unrecorded treatment.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Kanta_Hämeen_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:no_treatment_record",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Because the treatment categories overlap, Kanta-Häme's crude curative treatment share of 23.4% (95% CI 20.1–27.2; n=128/546) versus 27.0% (4009/14873) nationally and crude life-prolonging treatment share of 32.2% (95% CI 28.4–36.3; n=176/546) versus 30.4% (4522/14873) nationally have 95% confidence intervals that include the national values.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:curative:Kanta_Hämeen_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:curative",
          "cty:life_prolonging:Kanta_Hämeen_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:life_prolonging"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "While public data lack county waiting times, preliminary national averages show 155 days from symptoms to treatment in Finland versus 107 days in Sweden and 67 days in Denmark, comprising 56 days of patient delay, 41 days in primary care and 58 days in specialist care.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Symptoms",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start",
          "mot:total_fi",
          "mot:total_se",
          "mot:total_dk",
          "mot:patient",
          "mot:primary",
          "mot:specialist"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "how_sure_are_we": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "Public data report crude county shares without age or stage adjustment, reflect recording practices for treatments and MDT meetings, and omit pathway waiting times.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "fig:age_adjusted_only_kuva16",
        "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
        "bs:coverage:MDT",
        "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Taulukko 11 gives crude county shares without age adjustment; county-level age-adjusted curative shares appear only in a PNG figure (Kuva 16, by sex, with 95% CIs), where we have digitised national reference lines of 26.7% for men and 26.9% for women (±0.5 percentage points) but no digitised value for Kanta-Häme.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "fig:age_adjusted_only_kuva16",
          "k16:curative:men:national",
          "k16:curative:women:national"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "As a separate limitation, crude county shares cannot be stage-adjusted because stage at diagnosis is missing for about 48% of patients, and although a journal article shows HILMO diagnoses match the Cancer Registry for about 90% of most cancer types, that finding covers diagnosis concordance only, not treatment or MDT recording.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:7885b0974f",
          "lit:hilmo_90"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Kanta-Häme's crude recorded MDT share is 21.6% (95% CI 18.4–25.3; n=118/546) versus 6.0% (893/14873) nationally, with the 95% confidence interval excluding the national value, but HILMO procedures are entered only from direct patient contacts, so MDT figures measure recording practice rather than care.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Kanta_Hämeen_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "bs:coverage:MDT",
          "q:39e6ba43a9"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Public report data do not capture symptom onset or referrals, primary care visits are not included in the report's data, occupational health is not mentioned, imaging appears only as clinical diagnosis without tissue sampling in about 20% of patients, and specialist visits (93.6% within 12 months nationally) and treatments lack start dates.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Symptoms",
          "bs:coverage:Referral",
          "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
          "q:323de0d90d",
          "bs:coverage:Imaging",
          "q:5eb155decc",
          "bs:coverage:First_specialist_visit",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "what_to_do_first": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "The team recommends auditing stage, drug treatment and MDT recording completeness, tracking access times under THL 21/2016 definitions with handover alerts, and standardising referrals and diagnostic-phase contacts.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "rec:3",
        "rec:1",
        "rec:2",
        "thl:21_2016",
        "q:950a2f797b"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Because Kanta-Häme's crude no-treatment-record share is 32.1% (95% CI 28.3–36.1; n=175/546) versus 27.5% (4089/14873) nationally and national lung cancer data collection is incomplete without a cancer quality registry, the team recommends publishing county recording completeness for stage, drug treatment and MDT coding while the STM roadmap's measure 3.2.1 plans updating the quality-registry decree by 2026–2028.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:3",
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Kanta_Hämeen_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:no_treatment_record",
          "q:950a2f797b",
          "q:82d365cd2c",
          "q:47c7e11303",
          "q:f07a34a300",
          "q:f540c706f8"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Because the Health Care Act sets no maximum time for a cancer suspicion and national pathway monitoring is lacking, the team recommends reporting referral-to-treatment access times using THL guidance 21/2016 definitions for 16 cancers and flagging stalled handovers, while the Filha programme's diagnostics recommendation with recommended time limits is to be carried out before the 2030 mid-term evaluation.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:1",
          "law:no_max",
          "thl:21_2016",
          "q:ccda20dce9",
          "q:20d6ca414e",
          "q:432c0e51d6",
          "q:614febebf2",
          "q:14dff3e002"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Because patients are referred under local instructions and a mentor insight notes that weak referrals receive lower urgency ratings in specialist care, the team recommends adopting a standard referral content list and template modelled on KYS's regional pathway document, referring persistent unexplained symptoms for a pulmonologist assessment after a normal X-ray, and naming a diagnostic-phase contact person.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:2",
          "q:556431a0c2",
          "mentor:kaisa_referral",
          "reg:kys_template",
          "reg:kys_persistent",
          "reg:only_kys_xray",
          "reg:named_contact"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The team recommends these local steps while the STM roadmap plans standardised referral criteria and symptom-based models under measure 2.5.2 and national pathway descriptions with access times under measure 3.1.2 by 2026–2028 (all significant cancers by 2029–2031), plus measure 1.2.3 guidance on a named care-coordinator model by 2026–2028 for county adoption by 2029–2031.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:1",
          "rec:2",
          "q:0780bf74b0",
          "q:37bb4c3b38",
          "q:9a1cd194f5",
          "q:ed87906241",
          "q:0c7bf2dacb",
          "q:fc81032a80",
          "q:abcbb06ae3",
          "q:050ee09ebe"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
